IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cb3-seat`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act, Parts XI to XIV.1 -- worked cases for the seat layer (cb3-seat.l4).
--
-- Every case is a person asking one question with the facts they could state; the expected answer is written by hand
-- from the text of the section named in the comment, never copied from the encoding's output. Names are invented.
-- At least one case per question; the questions that return a number, a date or a possibly missing value are asserted
-- with EQUALS, and a question the text does not answer (the record date for voting when none is fixed) is asserted as NOTHING.

-- Maya is a director of Northfield Ltd, a distributing corporation: she is an insider (s 126(1)(a)).
#ASSERT `Am I an insider of a distributing corporation` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Dev is a shareholder with a small holding who has none of the four connections: he is not an insider by s 126(1).
#ASSERT NOT `Am I an insider of a distributing corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Lena is retained by the distributing corporation as its bookkeeper (s 126(1)(d)).
#ASSERT `Am I an insider of a distributing corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Maya is the president of Northfield Ltd, a body corporate.
#ASSERT `Am I an officer for the purposes of Part XI` `the president` TRUE `a body corporate`
-- Ravi was appointed an officer under section 121 but holds no office on the list and performs no similar function: not an officer for Part XI.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I an officer for the purposes of Part XI` `an officer appointed under section 121` TRUE `a body corporate`
-- A company performing functions like an office-holder is not an individual, so it is not an officer here.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I an officer for the purposes of Part XI` `another individual performing functions similar to those of one of these offices` FALSE `a body corporate`
-- Priya holds convertible debentures that she can convert today into voting shares: they count as a share.
#ASSERT `Is what I hold a share for the purposes of Part XI` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- Non-voting preferred shares, with no event giving them a vote, no conversion and no option, are not a share for Part XI.
#ASSERT NOT `Is what I hold a share for the purposes of Part XI` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Maya is a director of a holding company that controls 15 per cent of the voting rights; the regulations prescribe 10 per cent.
#ASSERT `Am I deemed an insider because my body corporate holds a large block of voting shares` TRUE 0.15 0.10
-- Exactly the prescribed percentage is not more than it.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I deemed an insider because my body corporate holds a large block of voting shares` TRUE 0.10 0.10
-- Ravi is an officer of the wholly owned subsidiary of a distributing corporation.
#ASSERT `Am I deemed an insider of the holding corporation because I run its subsidiary` TRUE TRUE
-- Ravi is an officer of a body corporate that is not a subsidiary of a distributing corporation.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I deemed an insider of the holding corporation because I run its subsidiary` TRUE FALSE
-- Priya owns 1,000 shares herself and controls two companies owning 4,000 and 2,500: she is deemed to own 7,500.
#ASSERT `How many shares am I deemed to own beneficially` 1000 (LIST 4000, 2500) EQUALS 7500
-- Priya controls no body corporate: only her own 1,000 shares count.
#ASSERT `How many shares am I deemed to own beneficially` 1000 EMPTY EQUALS 1000
-- Northfield Holdings owns 500 shares itself and its two affiliates own 100 and 200: it is deemed to own 800.
#ASSERT `How many shares is my body corporate deemed to own beneficially` 500 (LIST 100, 200) EQUALS 800
-- Maya, an insider, sells an option to buy shares of Northfield Ltd: that is a change in her beneficial ownership.
#ASSERT `Is my acquisition or disposition of an option treated as a change in my beneficial ownership` TRUE TRUE
-- Dev is not an insider: the deeming does not apply to him.
#ASSERT NOT `Is my acquisition or disposition of an option treated as a change in my beneficial ownership` FALSE TRUE
-- Maya, an insider, sells shares of Northfield Ltd that she does not own: barred.
#ASSERT `Am I barred from selling a security short` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- Maya sells shares she owns and has fully paid for: not a short sale.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I barred from selling a security short` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Maya sells shares she owns but has not fully paid for: also barred.
#ASSERT `Am I barred from selling a security short` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- Maya, an insider, buys a put on Northfield Ltd shares: barred.
#ASSERT `Am I barred from selling a call or buying a put` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- Maya does neither: not barred.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I barred from selling a call or buying a put` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- The call is on the securities of an unrelated company: not barred by s 130(2).
#ASSERT NOT `Am I barred from selling a call or buying a put` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Maya sold shares she did not own on 1 March 2027, but held options on them and delivered the shares two days later.
#ASSERT `Does the exception for owners of a convertible security or option apply to my sale` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2027 3 1) TRUE (YMD 2027 3 3) FALSE (YMD 2027 3 1)
-- Maya held nothing convertible: the exception does not apply.
#ASSERT NOT `Does the exception for owners of a convertible security or option apply to my sale` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2027 3 1) FALSE (YMD 2027 3 1) FALSE (YMD 2027 3 1)
-- Maya sold shares she did not own, held nothing she could deliver, and bought no put or call: guilty of the offence.
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of an offence for a short sale, call or put` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2027 3 1) FALSE (YMD 2027 3 1) FALSE (YMD 2027 3 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- The same sale, but Maya held options and delivered the shares two days later: the exception removes the contravention.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I guilty of an offence for a short sale, call or put` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2027 3 1) TRUE (YMD 2027 3 3) FALSE (YMD 2027 3 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Maya made a profit of $200,000: three times that is $600,000, so the $1,000,000 floor of the ceiling applies.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for a short sale, call or put` 200000 EQUALS 1000000
-- Maya made a profit of $500,000: three times that is $1,500,000, which is more than $1,000,000.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for a short sale, call or put` 500000 EQUALS 1500000
-- Maya made a profit of $200,000: the ceiling on imprisonment is six months.
#ASSERT `What is the longest imprisonment I can face for a short sale, call or put, in months` 200000 EQUALS JUST 6
-- Maya is a director of the corporation (s 131(1)(c)).
#ASSERT `Am I an insider of the corporation for section 131` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0.10
-- Priya holds 12 per cent of the voting rights where the regulations prescribe 10 per cent (s 131(1)(d)).
#ASSERT `Am I an insider of the corporation for section 131` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0.12 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0.10
-- Dev holds exactly the prescribed 10 per cent and has no other connection: not an insider by holding alone.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I an insider of the corporation for section 131` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0.10 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0.10
-- Lena was told confidential information by a director whom she knew to be one (s 131(1)(h)).
#ASSERT `Am I an insider of the corporation for section 131` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 0.10
-- Lena was told confidential information by a director but neither knew nor ought to have known that he was one: not (h).
#ASSERT NOT `Am I an insider of the corporation for section 131` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0.10
-- Priya bought a call option on the corporation's shares: deemed a security of the corporation.
#ASSERT `Does section 131 treat what I hold or traded as a security of the corporation` FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- A bond of an unrelated issuer whose price does not follow the corporation's: not a security of the corporation.
#ASSERT NOT `Does section 131 treat what I hold or traded as a security of the corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Northfield Holdings proposes a take-over bid for the corporation: deemed an insider.
#ASSERT `Am I deemed an insider because I propose a take-over bid or a business combination` TRUE FALSE
-- No bid and no business combination is proposed.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I deemed an insider because I propose a take-over bid or a business combination` FALSE FALSE
-- Maya is a director of the bidder (a person described in subsection (3)): paragraph (c) applies, read with the bidder for the corporation.
#ASSERT `Am I an insider because I am connected to a person who proposes a take-over bid or a business combination` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0.10 FALSE
-- Ravi is an affiliate of the bidder: an insider of the target by (3.1).
#ASSERT `Am I an insider because I am connected to a person who proposes a take-over bid or a business combination` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0.10 TRUE
-- Dev has no connection to the bidder.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I an insider because I am connected to a person who proposes a take-over bid or a business combination` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0.10 FALSE
-- Northfield Holdings proposes a take-over bid and obtained the information from the corporation: deemed insider with respect to it.
#ASSERT `Am I an insider of the corporation with respect to the confidential information` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0.10 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- The same bidder did not obtain the information from the corporation: (3) gives insider status only for information obtained from it.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I an insider of the corporation with respect to the confidential information` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0.10 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Maya is a director of the corporation: an insider under (1).
#ASSERT `Am I an insider of the corporation with respect to the confidential information` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0.10 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Ravi is a director of a person who proposes a take-over bid: an insider by (3.1) read with (1)(c).
#ASSERT `Am I an insider of the corporation with respect to the confidential information` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0.10 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Maya, a director, sold shares knowing that an unannounced takeover would raise the price, and she can establish none of the defences.
#ASSERT `Must I compensate the person I traded with because I traded on confidential information` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Maya reasonably believed the takeover had already been announced: defence (a) removes the liability.
#ASSERT NOT `Must I compensate the person I traded with because I traded on confidential information` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Maya knew nothing confidential when she traded: no liability under s 131(4).
#ASSERT NOT `Must I compensate the person I traded with because I traded on confidential information` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- The trade took place in circumstances the regulations prescribe: defence (c).
#ASSERT NOT `Must I compensate the person I traded with because I traded on confidential information` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Priya sold her shares to a director who knew of an unannounced takeover: she is owed compensation for her damages.
#ASSERT `Am I owed compensation by an insider who traded with me on confidential information` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- The insider can establish that Priya knew of the takeover too: defence (b).
#ASSERT NOT `Am I owed compensation by an insider who traded with me on confidential information` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- Maya must account to the corporation for the profit from her trade on the undisclosed takeover.
#ASSERT `Am I accountable to the corporation for the benefit I got from my trade` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- Maya establishes that she reasonably believed the takeover was public.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I accountable to the corporation for the benefit I got from my trade` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- As a director of the corporation, Dev asks whether the insider who traded must account for the profit: yes.
#ASSERT `Is an insider who traded accountable to my corporation for the benefit they got` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- The insider did not trade, only knew: nothing to account for under (5).
#ASSERT NOT `Is an insider who traded accountable to my corporation for the benefit they got` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- Maya told a friend about the unannounced takeover and the friend's buyer later bought from a seller: Maya is liable to that seller.
#ASSERT `Must I compensate someone because I disclosed confidential information` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Maya establishes that the disclosure was necessary in the course of her business (defence (c)): no liability.
#ASSERT NOT `Must I compensate someone because I disclosed confidential information` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- Northfield Holdings, a bidder (a person described in (3)), cannot rely on defence (c): the disclosure is not excused by ordinary business necessity.
#ASSERT `Must I compensate someone because I disclosed confidential information` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- The bidder establishes that the disclosure was necessary to effect the take-over bid: defence (d).
#ASSERT NOT `Must I compensate someone because I disclosed confidential information` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Priya sold her shares to a buyer who had been tipped by a director: she is owed compensation.
#ASSERT `Am I owed compensation because an insider disclosed confidential information that led to my trade` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Priya did not trade with anyone who received the tip: nothing is owed to her under (6).
#ASSERT NOT `Am I owed compensation because an insider disclosed confidential information that led to my trade` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Maya was paid for her tip: she must account to the corporation for the benefit.
#ASSERT `Am I accountable to the corporation for the benefit I got from disclosing confidential information` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Maya reasonably believed the information had been generally disclosed: defence (6)(a).
#ASSERT NOT `Am I accountable to the corporation for the benefit I got from disclosing confidential information` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- As a shareholder, Priya asks whether the director who tipped must account to the corporation for what she was paid: yes.
#ASSERT `Is an insider who disclosed confidential information accountable to my corporation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Priya's shares were shares of a distributing corporation: the court must consider the post-disclosure comparison.
#ASSERT `Must the court compare my price with the market price after disclosure` TRUE
-- The security is not of a distributing corporation: the court has no such duty under (8).
#ASSERT NOT `Must the court compare my price with the market price after disclosure` FALSE
-- Dev paid $120 a share and the twenty-day average after disclosure was $90: the court must consider $30 a share.
#ASSERT `As a purchaser, what amount must the court consider` 120 90 EQUALS 30
-- Priya sold at $110 and the twenty-day average after disclosure was $150: the court must consider $40 a share.
#ASSERT `As a seller, what amount must the court consider` 150 110 EQUALS 40
-- Two directors traded on the same information: their liability is joint and several.
#ASSERT `If several insiders are liable to me, is each liable for the whole` 2
-- Only one insider is liable: there is no joint liability to speak of.
#ASSERT NOT `If several insiders are liable to me, is each liable for the whole` 1
-- Priya discovered the facts on 1 March 2027: her last day is 1 March 2029.
#ASSERT `By when must I start my action under section 131` (YMD 2027 3 1) EQUALS (YMD 2029 3 1)
-- Priya starts her action on the last day: in time.
#ASSERT `May I still start my action under section 131` (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2029 3 1)
-- Priya starts her action the day after the last day: out of time.
#ASSERT NOT `May I still start my action under section 131` (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2029 3 2)
-- The by-laws name Toronto and the meeting is in Toronto: lawful.
#ASSERT `Is the place of the meeting lawful` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- The by-laws name no place, so the directors choose Calgary: lawful.
#ASSERT `Is the place of the meeting lawful` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- The by-laws name Toronto but the directors picked Calgary: not the place the by-laws provide.
#ASSERT NOT `Is the place of the meeting lawful` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- The directors picked a place outside Canada: not lawful under (1).
#ASSERT NOT `Is the place of the meeting lawful` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- The articles of Northfield Ltd specify New York for meetings.
#ASSERT `May the meeting be held outside Canada` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- Every voting shareholder has agreed to meet in Singapore.
#ASSERT `May the meeting be held outside Canada` TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- Not specified in the articles and not every voting shareholder agrees.
#ASSERT NOT `May the meeting be held outside Canada` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Priya flew to the meeting in New York and voted: she is taken to have agreed to its being held there.
#ASSERT `Am I taken to have agreed to a meeting held outside Canada because I attended` TRUE FALSE
-- Priya attended only to object that the meeting was not lawfully held: she is not taken to have agreed.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I taken to have agreed to a meeting held outside Canada because I attended` TRUE TRUE
-- Priya, a shareholder, joins the annual meeting by video link that the corporation provides.
#ASSERT `May I take part in the meeting by telephone or other electronic means` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- The by-laws provide otherwise: she may not take part by electronic means.
#ASSERT NOT `May I take part in the meeting by telephone or other electronic means` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- The corporation makes no facility available.
#ASSERT NOT `May I take part in the meeting by telephone or other electronic means` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- Priya joined by video link: she counts as present, for example towards a quorum.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as present at the meeting if I take part by electronic means` TRUE
-- She did not take part by such a facility: this deeming does not apply.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I treated as present at the meeting if I take part by electronic means` FALSE
-- Maya and the other directors call a virtual-only meeting and the by-laws allow it.
#ASSERT `May we hold the meeting entirely by electronic means` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- The by-laws do not provide for it: the directors cannot decide on a virtual-only meeting.
#ASSERT NOT `May we hold the meeting entirely by electronic means` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- Northfield Ltd came into existence on 15 January 2027: the last day to call its first annual meeting is 15 July 2028.
#ASSERT `By when must the directors call the first annual meeting` (YMD 2027 1 15) EQUALS (YMD 2028 7 15)
-- Existence on 31 August 2027: eighteen months later falls in February 2029, which has 28 days, so the last day is 28 February 2029.
#ASSERT `By when must the directors call the first annual meeting` (YMD 2027 8 31) EQUALS (YMD 2029 2 28)
-- Called on the last day: in time.
#ASSERT `Did the directors call the first annual meeting in time` (YMD 2027 1 15) (YMD 2028 7 15)
-- Called the day after the last day: late.
#ASSERT NOT `Did the directors call the first annual meeting in time` (YMD 2027 1 15) (YMD 2028 7 16)
-- The last meeting was on 30 June 2027 (fifteen months: 30 September 2028) and the financial year ended on 31 December 2027 (six months: 30 June 2028): the earlier, 30 June 2028, is the last day.
#ASSERT `By when must the directors call the next annual meeting` (YMD 2027 6 30) (YMD 2027 12 31) EQUALS (YMD 2028 6 30)
-- The financial year ended on 31 March 2027 (six months: 30 September 2027) and the last meeting was on 30 June 2027 (fifteen months: 30 September 2028): the earlier is 30 September 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must the directors call the next annual meeting` (YMD 2027 6 30) (YMD 2027 3 31) EQUALS (YMD 2027 9 30)
-- Called on the last day, 30 June 2028: in time.
#ASSERT `Did the directors call the next annual meeting in time` (YMD 2027 6 30) (YMD 2027 12 31) (YMD 2028 6 30)
-- Called on 1 July 2028: late, although within fifteen months of the last meeting.
#ASSERT NOT `Did the directors call the next annual meeting in time` (YMD 2027 6 30) (YMD 2027 12 31) (YMD 2028 7 1)
-- Maya and her co-directors call a special meeting to approve a sale.
#ASSERT `May the directors call a special meeting whenever they like` TRUE
-- A shareholder acting alone cannot call a special meeting under (2): see the requisition in section 143.
#ASSERT NOT `May the directors call a special meeting whenever they like` FALSE
-- Northfield Ltd applies for an extension because its accounts are not ready.
#ASSERT `May the corporation ask the court for more time to call the annual meeting` TRUE TRUE
-- A shareholder cannot make this application: it is the corporation's.
#ASSERT NOT `May the corporation ask the court for more time to call the annual meeting` FALSE TRUE
-- Maya and the directors fix 1 May as the record date in advance, in time.
#ASSERT `May the directors fix a record date` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- The date was not fixed in advance.
#ASSERT NOT `May the directors fix a record date` TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- Notice is given on 10 May 2027 and no record date was fixed: the record date for notice is the day before, 9 May 2027.
#ASSERT `What is the record date if the directors fix none` `a record date for receiving notice of a meeting of shareholders` TRUE (YMD 2027 5 10) (YMD 2027 6 15) (YMD 2027 5 1) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2027 5 9)
-- No notice is given: the record date is the day the meeting is held, 15 June 2027.
#ASSERT `What is the record date if the directors fix none` `a record date for receiving notice of a meeting of shareholders` FALSE (YMD 2027 5 10) (YMD 2027 6 15) (YMD 2027 5 1) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2027 6 15)
-- For a dividend the record date is the day the directors pass the resolution, 1 May 2027.
#ASSERT `What is the record date if the directors fix none` `a record date for receiving payment of a dividend` TRUE (YMD 2027 5 10) (YMD 2027 6 15) (YMD 2027 5 1) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2027 5 1)
-- The text gives no default record date for voting when none is fixed: the answer is "not covered".
#ASSERT `What is the record date if the directors fix none` `a record date for voting at a meeting of shareholders` TRUE (YMD 2027 5 10) (YMD 2027 6 15) (YMD 2027 5 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A record date is fixed and no waiver has been given by every holder.
#ASSERT `Must notice of the record date be given` TRUE FALSE
-- Every holder waived notice in writing.
#ASSERT NOT `Must notice of the record date be given` TRUE TRUE
-- No record date is fixed: no notice of it.
#ASSERT NOT `Must notice of the record date be given` FALSE FALSE
-- Advertised and notified the exchange, in time.
#ASSERT `Has notice of the record date been given as the Act requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- No written notice went to the stock exchange.
#ASSERT NOT `Has notice of the record date been given as the Act requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- Priya is a voting shareholder: the corporation must send her notice.
#ASSERT `Am I owed notice of the meeting` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Maya is a director: also owed notice.
#ASSERT `Am I owed notice of the meeting` FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- A creditor who is none of the three is not owed notice by this section.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I owed notice of the meeting` FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- A distributing corporation sent notice within the prescribed period.
#ASSERT `Was notice of the meeting sent in time` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- A private corporation whose by-laws specify a shorter period sent notice within it.
#ASSERT `Was notice of the meeting sent in time` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- A distributing corporation cannot use a shorter period: late.
#ASSERT NOT `Was notice of the meeting sent in time` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Dev bought his shares after the record date: no notice need be sent to him.
#ASSERT `Can the corporation leave me off the notice because I was not registered on the record date` FALSE
-- Priya was registered on the record date: she must be sent notice.
#ASSERT NOT `Can the corporation leave me off the notice because I was not registered on the record date` TRUE
-- Priya never received the notice, but she is entitled to vote: she keeps her vote.
#ASSERT `Do I keep my right to vote even though I did not receive notice` TRUE FALSE
-- A person who is not entitled to vote does not gain the right from this rule.
#ASSERT NOT `Do I keep my right to vote even though I did not receive notice` FALSE FALSE
-- Adjourned for 29 days: an announcement is enough.
#ASSERT `Can the adjourned meeting be announced at the meeting without a fresh notice` 29 FALSE
-- Adjourned for 30 days: fresh notice is needed.
#ASSERT NOT `Can the adjourned meeting be announced at the meeting without a fresh notice` 30 FALSE
-- The by-laws require notice of an adjourned meeting.
#ASSERT NOT `Can the adjourned meeting be announced at the meeting without a fresh notice` 10 TRUE
-- Thirty days or more: notice as for an original meeting.
#ASSERT `Must notice of the adjourned meeting be given as for an original meeting` 30
-- Fewer than thirty days: no such notice.
#ASSERT NOT `Must notice of the adjourned meeting be given as for an original meeting` 29
-- Adjourned for 91 days in aggregate: more than ninety, so subsection 149(1) applies.
#ASSERT `Does management have to send a new form of proxy for the adjourned meeting` 91
-- Adjourned for exactly ninety days: not more than ninety, so it does not.
#ASSERT NOT `Does management have to send a new form of proxy for the adjourned meeting` 90
-- At an annual meeting, approving a stock option plan is special business.
#ASSERT `Is this business special business` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- At an annual meeting, electing directors is ordinary business.
#ASSERT NOT `Is this business special business` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- At a special meeting everything is special business, even an election.
#ASSERT `Is this business special business` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- The notice describes the option plan and sets out the special resolution.
#ASSERT `Does the notice of meeting say what the Act requires about the business` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- The notice omits the text of the special resolution.
#ASSERT NOT `Does the notice of meeting say what the Act requires about the business` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- Only ordinary business: nothing more is required of the notice by (6).
#ASSERT `Does the notice of meeting say what the Act requires about the business` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Priya waives notice by email.
#ASSERT `May I waive notice of the meeting` TRUE
-- A person with no right to attend cannot waive notice.
#ASSERT NOT `May I waive notice of the meeting` FALSE
-- Priya turns up and takes part: she has waived notice.
#ASSERT `Does my attendance at the meeting waive notice` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- Priya attends only to object that the meeting was not lawfully called: no waiver.
#ASSERT NOT `Does my attendance at the meeting waive notice` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Priya has held 100 shares for the prescribed period, and 100 are required: she may submit a proposal.
#ASSERT `May I submit a proposal to the shareholders` TRUE 100 100 FALSE 100
-- Dev holds 40 shares but his supporters bring the total to 120, with their support: he may submit.
#ASSERT `May I submit a proposal to the shareholders` TRUE 40 120 TRUE 100
-- One share short: not eligible.
#ASSERT NOT `May I submit a proposal to the shareholders` TRUE 99 99 FALSE 100
-- Lena holds no shares entitled to be voted at an annual meeting.
#ASSERT NOT `May I submit a proposal to the shareholders` FALSE 500 500 FALSE 100
-- Priya raises, from the floor, a matter she could have proposed.
#ASSERT `May I discuss a matter at the annual meeting` TRUE TRUE
-- The matter is not one on which she could have submitted a proposal.
#ASSERT NOT `May I discuss a matter at the annual meeting` TRUE FALSE
-- Exactly the prescribed number held for the prescribed period.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to submit a proposal` 100 100 FALSE 100
-- The supporters' shares count only if the proposer has their support.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I eligible to submit a proposal` 99 500 FALSE 100
-- With their support the supporters' shares count.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to submit a proposal` 99 500 TRUE 100
-- Priya relies on her own holding and gives her name, address, shares and dates.
#ASSERT `Does my proposal carry the information the Act requires` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- Dev relies on supporters but omitted their names and addresses.
#ASSERT NOT `Does my proposal carry the information the Act requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- Priya's proposal is 120 words, her statement 230, and her details 80: the details do not count, so 350.
#ASSERT `How many words of mine count toward the word limit` 120 230 80 EQUALS 350
-- The corporation asked Priya for her share certificates within the prescribed period.
#ASSERT `Must I prove that I am eligible to submit a proposal` TRUE
-- The corporation did not ask in time.
#ASSERT NOT `Must I prove that I am eligible to submit a proposal` FALSE
-- Priya sent her broker's statement in time and it shows 100 shares held for the period.
#ASSERT `Have I met my duty to prove my eligibility` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Her proof was in time but did not show the holding.
#ASSERT NOT `Have I met my duty to prove my eligibility` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- The corporation never asked: nothing was owed.
#ASSERT `Have I met my duty to prove my eligibility` FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- A timely, relevant, first-time proposal: no excuse.
#ASSERT NOT `Is the corporation excused from circulating my proposal` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- The proposal arrived after the prescribed period.
#ASSERT `Is the corporation excused from circulating my proposal` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- The proposal is a personal grievance against a director.
#ASSERT `Is the corporation excused from circulating my proposal` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- The same proposal failed to get the prescribed support at a recent meeting.
#ASSERT `Is the corporation excused from circulating my proposal` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- Dev sold his shares before the day of the last meeting and the next meeting is within the prescribed period.
#ASSERT `Is the corporation excused from setting out my later proposal because I stopped holding shares` TRUE TRUE
-- The next meeting is outside the prescribed period.
#ASSERT NOT `Is the corporation excused from setting out my later proposal because I stopped holding shares` TRUE FALSE
-- Northfield Ltd solicits proxies and received Priya's proposal in good order: it must circulate it.
#ASSERT `Must the corporation circulate my proposal in its management proxy circular` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- A corporation that does not solicit proxies has no duty under (2).
#ASSERT NOT `Must the corporation circulate my proposal in its management proxy circular` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- The proposal was late: the corporation is excused.
#ASSERT NOT `Must the corporation circulate my proposal in its management proxy circular` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- The circular sets out Priya's proposal: the duty is met.
#ASSERT `Has the corporation done what s 137(2) requires of it for my proposal` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- The corporation neither set out nor attached the proposal and no exception applies: the duty is not met.
#ASSERT NOT `Has the corporation done what s 137(2) requires of it for my proposal` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- The proposal was late, so the corporation was not bound to circulate it: nothing outstanding.
